# PLAN-UI — Personae Mobile: replicate the messenger pane

**Reference (source of truth):** `~/Projects/hermes-desktop-plugins/personae/`
— `README.md` = the feature spec, `plugin.js` (8,365 lines) = the implementation.
**Target:** `~/Projects/personae-mobile/` (Expo/RN, TypeScript, expo-router).
**Status:** REV 3 — transport question answered from source (§0), connection-UI rebuild (§5) and
export log (§6) designed, open items listed (§8). **Plan for approval; no build started.**

---

## 0. The transport question — answered

**Finding 1 — the plugin is not a client of the HTTP API.** It runs *inside* the Electron app and
speaks the app's own RPC surface (`profiles.list`, `profiles.get_asset`, `profiles.configure`,
`session.{list,active_list,history,title,create,close,delete,archive,branch_stored}`,
`display.status`, `display.thumbnail`, `cron.manage`, `projects.list`), with pane state in the app
store under `messenger-*-v1` keys. "Replicate the pane" = rebuild that information architecture on
the phone and source each feature from whichever surface actually has it.

**Finding 2 — those RPC methods have an HTTP/WS home: `/api/ws` on the dashboard.**
`hermes_cli/web_routers/chat_ws.py:595` mounts `@router.websocket("/api/ws")` and hands it to
`tui_gateway.ws.handle_ws`, under the in-code comment *"Drives the same `tui_gateway.dispatch` surface
Ink uses over stdio so the dashboard can render structured metadata"*. That is the plugin's protocol.
Alongside it the dashboard already serves `GET /api/profiles`, `GET /api/profiles/sessions`,
`GET /api/profiles/sessions/sidebar` (batched rail payload incl. `profile_totals`),
`PATCH /api/sessions/{id}` `{unread}`, `/api/cron/*`, and `/api/display/ws`.

**Finding 3 — but it is gated, and the cheap token does not open it.**
`should_require_auth()` (`web_server.py:517`) is `host not in {localhost,127.0.0.1,::1}` — **any**
non-loopback bind is gated, and `allow_public`/`--insecure` has been ignored since the June 2026
hermes-0day campaign. In gated mode the in-process `_SESSION_TOKEN` is **explicitly rejected**
("a leaked `_SESSION_TOKEN` must not grant access", `web_server_chat.py:261`), and the
`X-Hermes-Session-Token` header path is loopback-only (`web_server.py:459`). The per-path bearer
mechanism (`register_token_route`, `token_auth.py:31`) is opt-in and currently covers exactly one
path in the whole tree: `/api/gateway/drain`.

**Finding 4 — a non-loopback dashboard *is* reachable by a native client, but it costs a login.**
`dashboard_auth/middleware.py:162-173` accepts a bearer access token on **every** REST route and
stamps `request.state.session`. The live provider set is `[{"name":"basic","supports_password":true}]`;
the flow is RFC 8252 for native apps — `/auth/native/authorize` → `/auth/native/token` (access +
refresh), `/auth/native/refresh` (rotation **with reuse detection** → refresh must be single-flight),
plus `/auth/password-login`. The WS leg additionally needs `POST /api/auth/ws-ticket` (auth-required)
→ single-use ticket, **30 s TTL**.

### Options

| | Phone needs | Parity | Cost |
|---|---|---|---|
| **A. Stay on `:9222`** (`platforms.api_server`) | one static api key | partial — 4 reads missing | cheapest today, you own parity forever |
| **B. Gated `:9119`, RFC 8252 native flow** | login + token store + single-flight refresh + per-connection WS tickets + 401-retry | **full** | one auth subsystem |
| **C. Loopback dashboard `:9118` + pinned token + Serve** ⭐ | **one static token** | **full** | one systemd unit + one Serve entry + the adapter |
| **D. Hybrid (both, mandatory)** | two auth systems | full | most — rejected |

**Recommendation: C.** Run a *second, dedicated* dashboard bound to loopback
(`hermes dashboard --host 127.0.0.1 --port 9118`) with `HERMES_DASHBOARD_SESSION_TOKEN` pinned, and
publish it on the tailnet with `tailscale serve --bg --https=10444 http://127.0.0.1:9118`.
Loopback ⇒ `auth_required` is False ⇒ the *simple* credential works everywhere again: the
`X-Hermes-Session-Token` header (or the legacy Bearer form) for REST, and the `token` query param for
the WS upgrade (`web_server_chat.py:366-371`). The app then speaks `/api/ws` — **the same protocol the
pane speaks** — and gets `profiles.list`, `profiles.get_asset` (avatars), `display.status` (the
live/blocked dot), `session.active_list`, `cron.manage`, `projects.list` as-is, plus REST for the rail.

This is the same shape Desktop uses for its own private loopback backend
(`_desktop_loopback_auth_exempt`, `web_server.py:541-560`). Nothing is hacked; the awkward login flow
only exists for non-loopback binds.

Leave the existing `0.0.0.0:9119` dashboard alone — that is the browser-login one. Keep option **A**
in the connectivity list as a *fallback candidate* (that code exists and is tested), not as primary.

**What this changes:** D2 (`/api/profiles`) and D3 (unread read-back) stop being upstream work —
they are consumed. The genuinely missing pieces shrink to: the exact amber semantics
(`display.status` vs the sidebar's "recently active" heuristic) and whether a session payload carries
the `last_read_at` watermark.
**What it does not change:** groups / colours / manual order / read markers stay phone-local — there
is no server-side `messenger-*` state at all, so D1(a) is the only option, not a preference.

---

## 1. What the app has today (the delta)

Roster (profile rows + day-grouped session rows, 25/page) · Thread (history, composer, SSE token
stream, working Stop) · Settings (base URL, key, extra profiles, model) · connectivity layer (ordered
route candidates by role+priority, Tailscale trigger module, honest failure taxonomy) · PT-PT
throughout · **60 offline tests** + `mock/` gateway (a build loop that runs with no phone and no key).
Shipped: `dist/personae-0.3.0.apk`, versionCode 3, same release key (upgrades in place over
0.1.0/0.2.0).

Everything below is what the plugin does and the app does **not**.

---

## 2. Parity matrix

### Bucket A — served; mobile just renders/acts

| Plugin feature | Endpoint |
|---|---|
| Profile → that profile's sessions, newest first | `GET /api/sessions` (`/p/<profile>/` prefix for extra profiles) |
| Open session, full history | `GET /api/sessions/{id}/messages` |
| Compose + streamed reply, **Stop** | `POST .../chat/stream` · `/chat` · `POST /v1/runs/{id}/stop` |
| New session with a profile | `POST /api/sessions` |
| Rename / pin / archive / hide | `PATCH /api/sessions/{id}` (title, pinned, archived, hidden) |
| Delete | `DELETE /api/sessions/{id}` |
| Fork / branch | `POST /api/sessions/{id}/fork` |
| Parent↔child links, ↳ / ↩ markers | `parent_session_id`, `_lineage_root_id` |
| Mark read/unread (**write**) | `PATCH {unread}` → `db.set_session_read` |
| Row body: preview, age, counts, tokens, cost | `preview`, `last_active`, `message_count`, `tool_call_count`, cost fields |
| Per-session model lock | `POST /api/sessions/{id}/model` · `GET /api/model/options` |
| Bell / cron surface | `/api/cron/jobs*` · `/api/cron/fire` |

### Bucket B — the gaps, re-sized by option C

| Feature | Before | Under C |
|---|---|---|
| **Profiles list** | no route → upstream | ✅ `profiles.list` / `GET /api/profiles` |
| **Cross-profile rail** | hand-typed | ✅ `GET /api/profiles/sessions/sidebar` (batched, with totals) |
| **Avatars / thumbnails** | RPC-only | ✅ `profiles.get_asset` over `/api/ws` |
| **Running / "blocked on you" dot** | RPC-only | ✅ `display.status` via `/api/display/ws` — verify on a live run whether it distinguishes *pending approval* from *recently active* |
| **Unread read-back** | write-only | ⚠️ confirm the session payload carries `last_read_at`; if not, a 3-line read-back |
| **Groups / colours / manual order / Apropos / Bots identity** | client store | ❌ phone-local (D1a) — desktop and phone will differ until a shared opaque blob exists |

### Bucket C — mobile builds it (no server question)

Expand/collapse a profile into its sessions · row geometry · long-press context menus (Open, Rename,
Colour, File into group, Sort, Copy id, Apropos, Delete) · multi-select + selection bar (bulk archive
/ delete / Apropos) · groups as drop targets · toolbar chrome (bell, **+**, folder+, search, filters)
· day grouping and pagination · status-dot aggregation (profile dot = aggregate of its sessions,
never its own) · PT-PT strings · theme.

**Search & filter is a trap:** the pane searches server-side over *profiles and sessions*. The REST
API takes only `source`, exact `title`, `include_children`, `include_hidden` — no text search, no
activity/kind/profile-set filters. Either filter client-side over the fetched page (say so in the UI)
or add one RPC method on `/api/ws`.

---

## 3. Touch mapping — the plugin's affordances are mouse-shaped

| Plugin (mouse) | Phone |
|---|---|
| Right-click context menu | Long-press → action sheet |
| Hover states | None — affordance always visible |
| Drag row between groups / reorder groups | Long-press to lift, drop targets highlight |
| Ctrl/Cmd-click multi-select | "Selecionar" from the toolbar; tap rows to tick |
| Scroll + 25/page pagination | `FlatList` (virtualised) |

In scope — without it, "all features" is not actually reachable on a phone.

---

## 4. Decisions

**Answered by you (2026-10-11):** D1 = (a) phone-local pane state · D2 = `/api/profiles` ·
D3 = close the gaps.

- **D4 — transport: option C** (dedicated loopback dashboard + pinned token + Serve). `:9222` demoted
  to a fallback candidate. Rejected: hybrid (two auth systems, zero benefit), gated `:9119` as-is
  (inherits a login/token/refresh/ticket subsystem).
- **D5 — avatars:** free under C (`profiles.get_asset`). Recommend taking them; initials monogram only
  if the WS asset path misbehaves.
- **D6 — keep the `:9222` path?** Yes, as an optional advanced fallback (code exists, tested). Not a
  second mandatory adapter.

---

## 5. Connection settings — rebuild it around "am I connected?"

Today Settings is a form: base URL, key, extra profiles, model, an insecure-route consent switch, a
route list with role+priority, four failure codes. That is the engineer's view. Replace with:

- **One state card**, three states: `Sem ligação` / `A ligar…` / `Ligado a personae-sk`.
- **A four-step checklist in plain PT-PT**, each row green/red and actionable:
  1. Rede — o telemóvel tem internet?
  2. Tailscale — está ligado? (button triggers the tunnel via the existing local module; on iOS the
     honest note stays, D7)
  3. Gateway — o dashboard responde?
  4. Autorização — o token foi aceite?
- **One primary button that fixes the first failing step** — deep-link to Tailscale, or retry, or ask
  for the token only when it is genuinely the problem. No dead ends.
- **"Testar ligação"** runs all four and prints a copyable result — the same payload the export log
  carries.
- **Advanced, collapsed by default:** route list, roles, priorities, timeouts, the insecure-route
  consent, the `:9222` fallback. A fresh install must need **zero** of it: host + token → connected.
- The honest failure reasons stay — below the friendly line, not instead of it.

---

## 6. Export log — one file, log + your description

- **Records:** a capped ring buffer (≈500 events) of structured entries — UTC timestamp, level,
  category (`net|auth|api|ws|ui|error`), message; per network call: method, path, status, duration,
  chosen route, attempt #.
- **Header block:** app version + versionCode, build id, device model + OS, active route + candidate
  list, dashboard host (host only), Tailscale state, last 3 failures.
- **A description box on the export screen** — what you type lands at the top of the file, so one
  file *is* "log + what went wrong" (your ask).
- **Share, don't upload:** write a `.txt` to the app cache dir and open the OS share sheet
  (`expo-sharing`) → WhatsApp / Gmail / Drive, plus copy-to-clipboard. Reachable from Settings **and**
  from the failure banner, where you would actually want it.
- **Redaction is mandatory and tested:** strip auth headers, api keys, access/refresh tokens, and
  `token`/`ticket`/`internal` query values → `[REDACTED]`. Never log request bodies carrying
  credentials. A unit test must assert a known secret cannot appear in an exported log — this rule
  rots silently otherwise.
- Local only. No telemetry, no auto-send.

---

## 7. Phases (each ends in a verifiable artifact)

- **P0 — transport.** Dashboard adapter (REST + `/api/ws`) behind the existing `src/api` interface;
  token in `expo-secure-store`; the loopback instance + Serve entry documented as setup. Extend
  `mock/` to serve the dashboard routes **and** a fake WS dispatch. `verify:` rail renders from
  `/api/profiles` + `/sidebar`; a scripted RPC call returns a profile asset; `:9118`-down falls back
  to the `:9222` candidate.
- **P1** expand/collapse the rail into per-profile sessions. `verify:` rows come from the API and the
  profile dot is an aggregate of its sessions.
- **P2** session actions via long-press + the Bucket-A write calls; `verify:` each against the mock,
  incl. 409/404 paths.
- **P3** toolbar, search/scope filters with the honest client-side boundary.
- **P4** groups + colours + manual sort on local state (D1a).
- **P5** multi-select bulk actions.
- **P6** Apropos (scoped).
- **P7** connection screen rebuild (§5) + export log (§6).
- **P8** iOS parity pass via EAS.

Every phase: git commit, `npm test` green (the 60 existing tests must stay green), `tsc --noEmit`
clean. Android first, then iOS.

